WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:03.260
♪ Beef dessert, beef dessert ♪

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.320
- Are you still rolling?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.970
- [Katie] Okay, Jasmine,
what are we doing today?

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.030
- I just finished watching
a clip from "Friends"

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.980
where Rachel makes this English Trifle,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.070
and I've wanted to make
this for a very long time.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.170
I've been very curious,

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.410
so I did some research to
see how we can make it.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:18.930
We're gonna make it
because I want to find out

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.150
if it's like a comedy TV show punchline,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.070
or if it's the real thing,
because Joey liked it.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.720
- What's not to like? Custard? Good.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.970
Jam? Good.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.120
Meat? GOOD.
(Audience laughs)

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.850
- And I think I might be a Joey.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.370
Then you guys said you
didn't want to try it

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:34.020
so I thought, well, we
should definitely do it.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.780
So today, we will be making
the Thanksgiving Trifle

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.620
from "Friends" where Rachel messes it up

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.600
and it's a half a Trifle,
half a Shepherd's Pie.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.940
Sounds pretty good. I'm excited.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.130
- [Katie] Are you dressed
as Rachel right now?

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.543
- I am! You noticed?

00:00:45.543 --> 00:00:48.330
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.170
We are gonna start by making the custard.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:51.400
Rachel makes it from scratch.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.520
I have a sauce pan over here.
I'm just adding in my milk.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.010
Now I'm gonna add a pinch
of salt and my sugar.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.660
Now we're just gonna whisk this together

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.690
until the sugar is melted.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.060
And then we want to keep this warm,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.710
we don't want it to come to a boil.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.220
So while this is warming, I
am going to make my slurry.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:08.720
I have some corn starch here

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.153
and I'm just going to add in my milk.

00:01:11.153 --> 00:01:12.160
Just going to whisk this together.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.000
So the slurry will help
thicken my custard.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.280
This is just a very
simple classic custard.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.140
Now we are going to separate some eggs.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.640
Let's hope this goes well.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.180
Or maybe you might catch a
Rachel moment right on camera.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.640
- [Katie] You're very serious
right now what happened?

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.490
- Am I very serious?

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.340
- [Katie] Yes, you seem
very, very concentrated.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.220
- You gotta be concentrated
when you're separating eggs

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.780
because...

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:35.610
Wow! That yolk is so much
bigger than the other one!

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.350
So, now I'm whisking up my egg yolks

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.410
and then we're gonna
temper it with my milk.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.910
So with tempering the eggs,

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:44.940
it just means that you're slowly
bringing up the temperature

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.060
so it doesn't cook and
become scrambled eggs

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.430
because that was one of
my Rachel mistakes before.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:53.640
Which is why I don't think she
really made it from scratch.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.610
- I made from scratch.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.430
- Now I'm adding my eggs,

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.370
my tempered eggs back into my milk.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.930
And then we can move on to the next step.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.610
So now that my egg is incorporated,

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.110
now I'm gonna add in my slurry.

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:07.890
I'm gonna slowly whisk
this for about five minutes

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.490
until it thickens up.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:10.860
So the custard is done.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:11.890
I've removed it from the heat,

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.050
and now we're gonna add in my butter.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.190
And then one teaspoon of vanilla.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.050
- [Katie] I think you're a Rachel.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:19.120
- You think I'm a Rachael?

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:19.953
- [Katie] A little bit.

00:02:19.953 --> 00:02:20.920
- I mean, I love her,

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.350
but I just don't think I am her.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.970
When we're doing our taste
tests, I feel like a Joey.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:26.870
All right. So my custard is done.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.870
I removed it from the heat
and we're just gonna run this

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.630
through a fine mesh strainer.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.690
So now I'm covering this
baby with saran wrap,

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:36.440
making sure to touch the custard,

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.220
to avoid getting that film on top,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.910
and then I'm gonna let
it cool a little bit

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.980
before putting it in the
fridge for a few hours.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:45.510
Now it's time to saute our
beef, peas, and onions.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.810
Be right back.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.990
I think this will taste
good. I have high hopes.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.240
So now we're going to make
the beef part of this dessert.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.960
It's supposed to be the Shepherd's Pie.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.030
So this is where Rachel gets it wrong.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.100
But you know what?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.310
I think this mixture is
actually not that bad.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.830
So I just added a splash
of some olive oil.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.470
So if you don't know
what Shepherd's Pie is,

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.730
it's like a meat pie,
but instead of a pie,

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.200
it's more like a casserole.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.850
And then it's topped with mashed potatoes.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:12.030
There's really nothing to not
like about Shepherd's Pie,

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.460
unless you mix it with
ladyfingers and jam.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.170
So I'm just going to saute these onions

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.460
until they're softened.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.640
I'm adding some salt, some
pepper, 'cause why not?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.690
All right, our onions have
softened a little bit,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:27.040
so now we are gonna add in the beef.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.450
- [Katie] Why do you like friends so much?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.520
- Aw, well, it's a really
good show. I really like it.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.280
But my mom, when she came to America,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.100
she would watch Friends to learn English.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.260
So, it has a very special
place in my heart.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.080
This beef is looking absolutely lovely.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.900
Now we're just going to
add in my frozen peas

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.730
and we're just going to fold this in.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.840
All right, this beef is
looking good for our dessert.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.220
I'm going to go gather
everything, get our custard,

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.490
and then we can get to assembling.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.100
So I have some ladyfingers.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.470
First, I'm going to line
them along the bottom.

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.450
Now I'm going to line the
side of the trifle dish.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.400
Our first layer is in!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.600
Next, we are going to go in with our jam.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.180
I put it in a piping bag.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.500
I'm trying to replicate the
little divots with the jam.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:10.610
I actually don't think
that the meat and jam combo

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.640
will be that weird.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.200
Jam is in, it's custard time.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.200
Let's go in with this layer of custard.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.380
- [Katie] Like, take out the beef,

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.490
do you think you'd like this now?

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.560
- [Jasmine] Yeah, if there was no beef,

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.960
this undoubtedly would be delicious.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.290
Next layer. The raspberries.

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.490
The raspberries are gonna
get buried anyway so,

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.450
just making sure that
it has its own layer.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:34.100
We're gonna go in with
another layer of ladyfingers

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.730
and it's time to go in with
the all-star ingredient, beef!

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.400
It actually doesn't look bad.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.960
Now we're gonna go in with
another layer of custard.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.320
Honestly, I feel pretty
good about this recipe.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.440
- [Katie] Wow.
- [Jasmine] I'm not gonna lie.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.880
It's banana time.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:49.820
- [Katie] How do you
feel about the banana,

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.710
meat, custard combo?

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.380
- Actually, it's pretty common

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.770
to eat banana with some savory dishes,

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.070
or like all dishes for some cultures.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:04:59.980
So it's not actually that weird to me.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:03.350
Last layer, y'all. The
whipped topping. Oh yeah.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:04.690
Let's just use the whole thing.

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:07.410
Oh, my gosh. This is beautiful.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.320
- [Katie] Yeah.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.560
- Hey!

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.710
You will eat it,

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.930
and you will like it!

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.100
All right, okay, I think we're done!

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.540
I'm gonna put this in the fridge,

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.050
let it sit for a few hours,

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.030
let the ladyfingers soften,

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.870
and then it's mealtime!

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:21.703
Can I get a woo?

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:24.160
- [Staff] Woo.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:26.160
- First person we're
bringing in today is Adrian,

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.750
Tasty's production coordinator

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.030
and a Friends super fan.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.370
Adrian has no idea this is happening.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.243
So let's bring them in!

00:05:32.243 --> 00:05:33.800
- I'm going to get Adrian.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.633
Adrian.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:35.640
- Yeah?

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.473
Hey.

00:05:36.473 --> 00:05:38.972
- [Katie] Do you want to
come taste some "Friends"...?

00:05:38.972 --> 00:05:39.805
- Yes!

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.020
- [Katie] What shirt are you wearing?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.520
- How you doin'?
(Katie laughs)

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.770
- [Jasmine] When you're
ready, open your eyes!

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:45.603
- [Adrian] Whoa!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.070
You have no idea how much
